  "calibration_analysis_findings": {
    "is_probability_blending_supported": true,
    "rationale": "Both models exhibit monotonic precision behavior across the upper probability range (>0.80). However, Full-Universe HardNeg exhibits lower mean negative scores (sharper rejection) due to exposure to 10.32M target distractors during training. A linear score combination S = alpha*P_hn + (1-alpha)*P_fu is well-behaved, with optimal weights in alpha in [0.85, 0.90] preserving the strong true-positive recall of HardNeg 1x while incorporating the conservative false-positive suppression of Full-Universe HardNeg."
